## What Problem This Solves

Fixes an issue where users or plugin authors writing Markdown command, hook, skill, or skill-workshop proposal files could have content starting with non-delimiter dash prefixes such as `---not` or `----` interpreted as YAML frontmatter when the file was just ordinary Markdown.

## Why This Change Was Made

The shared frontmatter parser now recognizes only full delimiter lines as frontmatter fences, after BOM and line-ending normalization. Claude bundle command prompt stripping and skill-workshop proposal extraction/stripping now use the same exact delimiter-line contract, so metadata parsing and body extraction do not drift through copied prefix checks.

## User Impact

Markdown content that starts with dash-prefixed text is preserved as body text unless it starts with a real `---` delimiter line. Valid frontmatter blocks continue to parse, and command plus workshop proposal paths no longer lose body content on the `---not` edge case.

## Evidence

- Refreshed branch against current `upstream/main` and pushed exact head `bfde24c890259d81e68f67dc31e54fc8688aa9e2`.
- Real command-loading proof: created a temporary Claude bundle plugin with a command Markdown file beginning with `---not`, then loaded it through `loadEnabledClaudeBundleCommands()` using a temporary `OPENCLAW_HOME`, temporary workspace, `plugins.load.paths`, and the production bundle command loader.

  Command:

  ```bash
  node --import tsx --input-type=module <<'EOF'
  import fs from 'node:fs';
  import os from 'node:os';
  import path from 'node:path';
  import { loadEnabledClaudeBundleCommands } from './src/plugins/bundle-commands.ts';

  const root = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'openclaw-frontmatter-proof-'));
  const home = path.join(root, 'home');
  const workspaceDir = path.join(root, 'workspace');
  const pluginRoot = path.join(root, 'proof-bundle');
  fs.mkdirSync(path.join(pluginRoot, '.claude-plugin'), { recursive: true });
  fs.mkdirSync(path.join(pluginRoot, 'commands'), { recursive: true });
  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(pluginRoot, '.claude-plugin', 'plugin.json'), JSON.stringify({ name: 'proof-bundle', commands: 'commands' }, null, 2));
  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(pluginRoot, 'commands', 'dash-prefix.md'), ['---not', 'name: nope', '---not', 'Treat this as command Markdown.', ''].join('\n'));
  fs.mkdirSync(workspaceDir, { recursive: true });
  process.env.OPENCLAW_HOME = home;
  process.env.OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR = path.join(home, '.openclaw');
  process.env.OPENCLAW_DISABLE_PERSISTED_PLUGIN_REGISTRY = '1';
  const cfg = {
    plugins: {
      load: { paths: [pluginRoot] },
      entries: {
        'proof-bundle': { enabled: true },
      },
    },
  };
  const commands = loadEnabledClaudeBundleCommands({ workspaceDir, cfg });
  console.log(JSON.stringify({ count: commands.length, commands: commands.map(({ rawName, description, promptTemplate }) => ({ rawName, description, promptTemplate })) }, null, 2));
  EOF
  ```

  Output:

  ```json
  {
    "count": 1,
    "commands": [
      {
        "rawName": "dash-prefix",
        "description": "---not",
        "promptTemplate": "---not\nname: nope\n---not\nTreat this as command Markdown."
      }
    ]
  }
  ```

  This shows the real command loader preserved the `---not` Markdown as command body text instead of parsing it as frontmatter.
- Workshop regression coverage now verifies `renderProposalMarkdown()` and `stripProposalFrontmatterForSkill()` preserve `---not` Markdown instead of extracting or stripping it as proposal frontmatter.
- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs packages/markdown-core/src/frontmatter.test.ts src/plugins/bundle-commands.test.ts src/hooks/frontmatter.test.ts src/skills/loading/frontmatter.test.ts src/skills/workshop/frontmatter.test.ts` passed: 2 Vitest shards, 5 test files, 47 tests.
- `./node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check --threads=1 packages/markdown-core/src/frontmatter.ts packages/markdown-core/src/frontmatter.test.ts src/plugins/bundle-commands.ts src/plugins/bundle-commands.test.ts src/hooks/frontmatter.test.ts src/skills/loading/frontmatter.test.ts src/skills/workshop/frontmatter.ts src/skills/workshop/frontmatter.test.ts` passed.
- `git diff --check` passed.
- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local` passed earlier with no accepted/actionable findings; this follow-up only applies the same delimiter-line rule to the workshop proposal helpers plus focused regression coverage.
- Attempted `pnpm check:changed -- packages/markdown-core/src/frontmatter.ts packages/markdown-core/src/frontmatter.test.ts src/plugins/bundle-commands.ts src/plugins/bundle-commands.test.ts src/hooks/frontmatter.test.ts src/skills/loading/frontmatter.test.ts`; local pnpm deps-status entered `pnpm install` and stalled on optional platform package downloads before checks started, so I interrupted it and left broader check coverage to PR CI.
- Related open candidate PRs for #101769 at proof refresh time: #101797 and #101803. Maintainers should land one canonical fix and close the rest after selection.

Closes #101769

